# M3 display wall, route 2 (fbdev): give the guest a /dev/fb0 so the redroid
# composer + gralloc stop dying on framebuffer ENOENT.
#
# Why FB_VIRTUAL: the redroid HWC/gralloc only speak framebuffer
# (hw_get_module("hwcomposer") fails -> "falling back to gralloc module" ->
# open /dev/graphics/fb%u -> /dev/fb%u -> mmap + FBIOPUT_VSCREENINFO; no
# drm/gbm/vsock path exists in either .so -- verified 2026-10-02 by strings +
# disasm of composer@2.1-service and gralloc.redroid.so from the device image).
# FB_VIRTUAL ("ONLY FOR TESTING", unswappable kernel memory, no visible output)
# is exactly the shape we need: gralloc mmaps it, HWC inits against it, SF gets
# its IComposer/default and stops LOG(FATAL). Display pixels come later via the
# app side reading the same memory (the vfb buffer is kernel memory; a second
# step can expose it). UML has no DT/platform-device problem here: vfb creates
# its own platform device at init, and menuconfig FB has no !UML dependency
# (only odd drivers like UVESA exclude UML). Enable with video=vfb: on the
# guest kernel command line.
#
# Risk on record: vfb_probe uses vmalloc_32_user (GFP_VMALLOC32 -> ZONE_DMA32);
# on UML without ZONE_DMA32 this degrades to NORMAL via the OPT_ZONE fallback
# in gfp.h (no NULL from the flag itself). If register_framebuffer or the
# remap_vmalloc_range mmap misbehaves under UML, that is the first suspect.
#
# UML gate: the whole fbdev menu sits under `if HAS_IOMEM`, and UML defaults
# to NO_IOMEM=y (HAS_IOMEM off). UML_IOMEM_EMULATION provides readl/writelock
# via INDIRECT_IOMEM so HAS_IOMEM subsystems build without dragging in a PCI
# bus (the usbcore precedent). vfb itself never touches MMIO -- plain
# vmalloc memory + platform device -- but Kconfig needs the gate open.
CONFIG_UML_IOMEM_EMULATION=y
CONFIG_FB=y
CONFIG_FB_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_FB_VIRTUAL=y
